From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:26:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Deprecate unsupported Remix resource memory limits without
 config writes

Remove the module-open SetMemoryLimits call and keep the legacy Lua API as a
documented no-op. Log once per module lifetime while preserving number checks
and its true return value. Never substitute User-layer budget settings.

Add an offline regression covering concurrent calls, disconnected Remix and
Lua compatibility. The prior oversized-skinning policy test still passes.

Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6.1-sol) <noreply@openai.com>
